    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\n ![](https://huggingface.co/avatars/27a10fb120f2cdbb7fb3215206f2b971.svg) ⟨28⟩\nARC-Ant⟨28⟩\n/\nAnnoy-PyEdu-Rs-Raw⟨29⟩\nlike 0\n Dataset card ⟨29⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨30⟩ Community ⟨31⟩\nThe dataset is currently empty. Upload or create new data files⟨30⟩. Then, you will be able to explore them in the Dataset Viewer.\n**YAML Metadata Warning:** empty or missing yaml metadata in repo card\nCheck out the documentation⟨32⟩ for more information.\n#   ⟨33⟩ Annoy: This should be a paper Title \n📑 Paper⟨34⟩ | 🌐 Project Page⟨35⟩ | 💾 Released Resources⟨36⟩ | 📦 Repo⟨37⟩\nWe release the raw data for our processed PythonEdu-Rs dataset, adopted from the original dataset from HuggingFaceTB team.\nThe data format for each line in the `0_368500_filtered_v2_ds25.sced.jsonl` is as follows:\n\n```\n{\n  \"problem_description\": <the problem description of the function>,\n  \"io_requirements\": <the input/output requirements and constraints>,\n  \"refcode\": <the reference code, including imported packages (optional), auxiliary functions (optional) and main entrypoint function>,\n  \"funcname\": <the function name for the entrypoint function>,\n  \"ios\": [\n    {\n      \"input\": <the input arguments>,\n      \"output\":<the returned value>\n    },\n    ...\n  ],\n  \"source\": <the source of the raw code files>,\n  \"category\": <the reasoning type we assign to this sample>,\n  \"meta\": <meta information about this sample>\n}\n\n```\n\nSome of the `ios` are empty. The reason is that when executing the code, the input/output sizes are too large and exceed our required constraints. Thus, they are not stored or used later.\n*Note: Due to imperfect LLM-based transformations, some problem descriptions do not contain enough information to describe the code. We leave this as future work to further enhance our data and update it to a better version.\nCopy to bucket new \n\nDownloads last month\n    81\nTotal file size: 4.25 kB\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨38⟩ Privacy⟨39⟩ About⟨40⟩ Careers⟨41⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
